TRASH.

definition: def"
Repository-local disposal boundary for CE-OS.

Nothing below trash is authoritative source.

All CE-OS-owned transient files, temporary test trees, generated scratch,
patch staging, probe output, intermediate edits, and other disposable
working material belong under trash/tmp rather than host-global temporary
storage or incidental repository paths.

Files deliberately removed from active authority but intentionally retained
for a bounded period belong under trash/retired.

Unclassified or suspicious material discovered during cleanup belongs under
trash/recovered until ownership is established.

The repository root is an authority surface and must remain immaculate.
Incidental artifacts are forbidden at repository root.
";

paths: (
temporary- "trash/tmp";
retired- "trash/retired";
recovered- "trash/recovered";
);

authority: (
root- false;
tmp- false;
retired- false;
recovered- false;
);

rules: (
self_contained- "CE-OS-owned disposable filesystem activity remains inside ~/ce-os";
root_immaculacy- "The ~/ce-os root may contain only intentional top-level architecture and authority surfaces";
root_creation- "Creation of a new repository-root file or directory requires explicit architectural purpose";
scratch- "Tools, agents, tests, scripts, and development workflows must not use repository root as scratch space";
temporary- "CE-OS temporary files and directories use ~/ce-os/trash/tmp";
host_tmp- "CE-OS-authored code must not rely on host-global /tmp or default host temporary directories";
retired- "Intentionally displaced material may be retained under trash/retired";
recovered- "Unowned cleanup discoveries are quarantined under trash/recovered";
tmp_cleanup- "trash/tmp may be cleared without preservation review";
other_cleanup- "trash/retired and trash/recovered require classification before permanent deletion";
generated_builds- "Tool-managed temporary content already contained inside an approved ignored build tree may remain inside that build tree";
git- "Track trash policy surfaces while ignoring disposable payloads";
);
